-- title:
--   Admissible evaluation extends to the reduced full modular function field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ belongs to the non-units of $A$; write $\kappa_A$ for its residue field. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the field $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ of the level-$M'$ full modular function field with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa_A\,M' = \kappa_A(j_q,j_{q,M'})$: that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto that target with kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $x \mapsto x \bmod \mathfrak m_A$ on constants (with $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,x$ integral exactly when $x \in A$), allowing every non-zero element to be scaled by a constant so as to have non-zero residue, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with orders of functions. Assume moreover ($h_{R_0}$) that each Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is $R_0$-integral with residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo $\mathfrak m_A$. Let $\mathcal A$ be a subring of $\mathbb Q$-Laurent series consisting exactly of those $gf$ which lie in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$, whose image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, and which satisfy $\mathrm{ord}_P(gf) \ge 0$ at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\mathrm{ord}_P(j_q) \ge 0$; assume $j_q \in \mathcal A$. Finally let $\Omega$ be a field equipped with a $\kappa_A$-algebra structure and $\mathrm{val} : \mathcal A \to \Omega$ a ring homomorphism which annihilates every element of $\mathcal A$ whose $R_0$-residue vanishes and for which $\mathrm{val}(j_q)$ is transcendental over $\kappa_A$. Then there is a $\kappa_A$-algebra homomorphism $\mathrm{emb}$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa_A\,M'$, the $\kappa_A$-subfield of $\kappa_A$-Laurent series generated by the divisor expansions, into $\Omega$ such that for every $gf \in \mathcal A$ one has $\mathrm{emb}$ applied to the image of $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(gf)$ under the inclusion of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa_A\,M'$ into $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa_A\,M'$ equals $\mathrm{val}(gf)$.
--
--   This is the field-theoretic extension step in the study of the reduction of modular curves of level $M'$ at a prime $q$ not dividing $M'$: an evaluation defined only on the ring of admissible rational level-$M'$ functions, compatible with the constant reduction $R_0$ and transcendental on $j$, is extended to a $\kappa_A$-embedding of the characteristic-$q$ full modular function field into $\Omega$. It is used in the construction of such embeddings from rigid data attached to a Tate point in the $\Gamma_1$-setting, and its proof cites the corresponding linear-relation and integrality statements over $R_0$ together with a general criterion for extending a map to an adjoined subalgebra.
